  "project_description": "Seeds SEO is a starter (metapackage) module from the Seeds distribution whose only job is to pull in and enable a curated stack of SEO modules so a new Drupal site gets a sensible SEO baseline in one step. The module itself ships no PHP code, routes, services, or configuration; it is a dependency aggregator. Enabling it turns on metatag (plus the Facebook and Open Graph submodules), simple_sitemap, redirect, pathauto, link_attributes, and length_indicator, while its composer.json additionally requires other SEO-related projects (fast_404, google_analytics, google_tag, yoast_seo, schema_metatag, ms_clarity, linkchecker) into the codebase for optional use.",
